      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Erieview Park, started in 1945, grew to include nine adult and nine children rides, including the Fright Zone dark ride.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneva-on-the-Lake%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Jennie Munger Gregory Museum, originally a boarding house, now preserves early vacation homes like Idle‑A‑While and Shady Beach Inn.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneva-on-the-Lake%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Geneva‑on‑the‑Lake sits on Lake Erie’s southern shore, 46 miles northeast of Cleveland, part of the Ashtabula micropolitan area.",
